-- title:
--   Galois representation over the Taylor–Wiles Hecke ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, and let $p$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline k$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$; let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N\neq 0$, let $r$ be a prime with $r\nmid N$ and $p\nmid r-1$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $P$ for $\ell$ (i.e. $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup and acts as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$), the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct nonzero primes outside $S$ and different from $r$, for each $i$ let $\pi_{\Delta,i}\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)})$ be a homomorphism and $\alpha_i\in k$, and let $\mathrm{cyc}_i\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times$ be the mod-$q_i$ cyclotomic character, characterised by $\sigma\mu=\mu^{(\mathrm{cyc}_i\sigma).\mathrm{val}}$ for all $q_i$-th roots of unity $\mu$. Put $L=$ `level N r qv` $=N\,(\prod_i q_i)\,r$ and let $H_Q=$ `HQ N r qv p πΔ` be the subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ obtained by intersecting `HR N r qv`, the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$, with the kernel of the homomorphism assembled from the $\pi_{\Delta,i}$. Assume `OpComm` and `DiaComm`: the Hecke operators at level $L$ with subgroup $H_Q$ commute with one another, and the diamond operators commute with them. Let $T=$ `HeckeRing N r qv S 𝒪 (HQ N r qv p πΔ) θ α` be the resulting $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of the endomorphism ring of the localised module `ML`, generated by the Hecke and diamond operators, and assume that $T$ is local, Noetherian, adically complete for its maximal ideal, finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, that $\mathcal O\to T$ is a local homomorphism, and that $\mathcal O\to T\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,T$ is surjective. Then there exists a Galois representation $\rho'$ over $T$, that is, a free $T$-module $V$ of rank two with a monoid homomorphism $\rho'\colon\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to\mathrm{End}_T V$ that is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension of $\mathbb Q$ fixes $V$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^n V$), with the following four properties. First, for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, every valuation subring $P$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $P$ for $\ell$, $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho'(\sigma)=$ `HeckeRing.T … ℓ`. Second, for all $n$, $\sigma$ and $a$ such that $\sigma\mu=\mu^a$ for every $p^n$-th root of unity $\mu$, and every unit $u$ of $\mathbb Z/L$ lying in `HR N r qv` whose image under each $\pi_{\Delta,i}\circ(\text{reduction mod }q_i)$ agrees with $\pi_{\Delta,i}(\mathrm{cyc}_i\sigma)$, the element $\det\rho'(\sigma)-a\,\langle u\rangle$ lies in the ideal of $T$ generated by $p^n$, where $\langle u\rangle=$ `HeckeRing.diamond … u`. Third, the residual representation of $\rho'$, over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,T$, is isomorphic as a Galois module to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Fourth, for every prime $\ell\nmid L$ with $\ell\neq p$, $\rho'$ is unramified at $\ell$: $\rho'(\sigma)=1$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of any valuation subring over $\ell$.
--
--   This is the existence of the modular two-dimensional Galois representation attached to the maximal ideal of the Hecke ring at Taylor–Wiles level $\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)\cap\Gamma_H(Q)$, in the normalisation where the determinant is the cyclotomic character times the diamond character and the trace of Frobenius at $\ell$ is $T_\ell$. It feeds the construction of Galois representations on the endomorphism ring of the localised cohomology module `ML` used in the patching argument.
